    "result_text": "The full build succeeds. `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and it passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the audit-logging requirement in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java` (the owner create handler, `addOwner`):\n\n1. Added SLF4J imports and a dedicated static logger named `AUDIT`:\n   ```java\n   private static final Logger AUDIT = LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"AUDIT\");\n   ```\n\n2. After a successful create (`saveOwner`), emit an audit line carrying the owner id, customerCode, and registrationDate:\n   ```java\n   AUDIT.info(\"owner created: id={} customerCode={} registrationDate={}\",\n       owner.getId(), owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate());\n   ```\n\nThe line is emitted only on the successful-create path (after all validation and the `saveOwner` call), so failed/rejected creates produce no audit entry. The `registrationDate` is logged via `LocalDate`'s ISO `toString()`, which matches the JSON serialization the test compares against. `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
